[{:db/id "3fb015f5-5a0e-5d78-85c8-9bb2368af69d" :answer/id #uuid "3fb015f5-5a0e-5d78-85c8-9bb2368af69d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=C + \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e8bad0ce-f595-50d5-af1a-7fffa40a1d48" :answer/id #uuid "e8bad0ce-f595-50d5-af1a-7fffa40a1d48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + 2 x + 14}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "83105ce1-a627-537e-90fa-45472b86b72a" :answer/id #uuid "83105ce1-a627-537e-90fa-45472b86b72a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=C + \\left|{x + 7}\\right|^{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ce90e750-d37b-538c-ba68-db863eb52201" :answer/id #uuid "ce90e750-d37b-538c-ba68-db863eb52201" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C - \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "50b41076-bc6b-5adf-a489-2df6a1b6896c" :answer/id #uuid "50b41076-bc6b-5adf-a489-2df6a1b6896c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "eddef3a2-c678-55ce-b1af-956ae057b5f5" :answer-field/id #uuid "eddef3a2-c678-55ce-b1af-956ae057b5f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["3fb015f5-5a0e-5d78-85c8-9bb2368af69d" "e8bad0ce-f595-50d5-af1a-7fffa40a1d48" "83105ce1-a627-537e-90fa-45472b86b72a" "ce90e750-d37b-538c-ba68-db863eb52201" "50b41076-bc6b-5adf-a489-2df6a1b6896c"] :answer-field/correct "50b41076-bc6b-5adf-a489-2df6a1b6896c" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "e1bf8ae5-5934-5cc9-9596-ee1587453d65" :question/id #uuid "e1bf8ae5-5934-5cc9-9596-ee1587453d65" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2(x+7)}{3{y}^{2}}.$ Assume $x+7>0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2(x+7)}{3{y}^{2}} \\\\ 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2(x+7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2(x+7)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2(x+7)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2(x+7)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={(x+7)}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={(x+7)}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{{(x+7)}^{2}+C}.\n$$\n\nUse the real cube root, on intervals where $y\\ne 0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["eddef3a2-c678-55ce-b1af-956ae057b5f5"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "4c6099ee-3b46-5070-8667-d71d5f0c9b4a" :answer/id #uuid "4c6099ee-3b46-5070-8667-d71d5f0c9b4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=C + \\frac{\\sqrt{10} \\left(x - 4\\right)^{2}}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "58c86c6d-7619-5b7c-b416-96c1c1700e10" :answer/id #uuid "58c86c6d-7619-5b7c-b416-96c1c1700e10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C + \\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{2}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "296f39b6-dbd2-59f0-a5e9-b253bd51c990" :answer/id #uuid "296f39b6-dbd2-59f0-a5e9-b253bd51c990" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C - \\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{2}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "10ae2311-48e4-512d-bc98-e93ee56b201e" :answer/id #uuid "10ae2311-48e4-512d-bc98-e93ee56b201e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=C + \\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "54fc91e8-26b5-58b2-83d7-c34a6bd9e3bc" :answer/id #uuid "54fc91e8-26b5-58b2-83d7-c34a6bd9e3bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C + 10 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "efb1736c-eeee-5a04-88e4-57a3ff9c1730" :answer-field/id #uuid "efb1736c-eeee-5a04-88e4-57a3ff9c1730" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["4c6099ee-3b46-5070-8667-d71d5f0c9b4a" "58c86c6d-7619-5b7c-b416-96c1c1700e10" "296f39b6-dbd2-59f0-a5e9-b253bd51c990" "10ae2311-48e4-512d-bc98-e93ee56b201e" "54fc91e8-26b5-58b2-83d7-c34a6bd9e3bc"] :answer-field/correct "58c86c6d-7619-5b7c-b416-96c1c1700e10" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "16bf90c3-d378-588a-9105-03dc1e2fe7d8" :question/id #uuid "16bf90c3-d378-588a-9105-03dc1e2fe7d8" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}}{y}.$ Assume $x-4>0.$ Take both sign branches on intervals where the radicand is positive and $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}}{y} \\\\ y\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\int 5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int 5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\frac{y^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^{2}}{2}=\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{4}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y^2 & =\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{2}+2C \\\\ y & =\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{2}+2C} \\\\ y & =\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{2}+K}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=2C$ is an arbitrary real constant. Use either sign consistently on each interval where the radicand is positive." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["efb1736c-eeee-5a04-88e4-57a3ff9c1730"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "d2892e08-e36f-52af-b525-ad4181822f25" :answer/id #uuid "d2892e08-e36f-52af-b525-ad4181822f25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=C + \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "55f667be-d4d4-5b14-b0fd-af942503ac45" :answer/id #uuid "55f667be-d4d4-5b14-b0fd-af942503ac45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\ln{\\left(C + \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2} \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1c425710-1266-581c-9722-fa8759833776" :answer/id #uuid "1c425710-1266-581c-9722-fa8759833776" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=C + \\ln{\\left(\\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2} \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "0f2d4e20-8550-5507-a465-b5397eb28c15" :answer/id #uuid "0f2d4e20-8550-5507-a465-b5397eb28c15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\ln{\\left(C - e^{- 2 x} \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4a018cae-2c2d-5c98-a82e-2dc47956d7c2" :answer/id #uuid "4a018cae-2c2d-5c98-a82e-2dc47956d7c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\ln{\\left(C - \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2} \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "88407400-d880-51d2-a70f-2e5e595f4faa" :answer-field/id #uuid "88407400-d880-51d2-a70f-2e5e595f4faa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["d2892e08-e36f-52af-b525-ad4181822f25" "55f667be-d4d4-5b14-b0fd-af942503ac45" "1c425710-1266-581c-9722-fa8759833776" "0f2d4e20-8550-5507-a465-b5397eb28c15" "4a018cae-2c2d-5c98-a82e-2dc47956d7c2"] :answer-field/correct "55f667be-d4d4-5b14-b0fd-af942503ac45" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "c36638cc-24f6-505b-b8ac-375828a36d26" :question/id #uuid "c36638cc-24f6-505b-b8ac-375828a36d26" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=- e^{- 2 x - y}.$ Work on intervals where the logarithm argument is positive." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =- e^{- 2 x - y} \\\\ e^{y}\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =- e^{- 2 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int e^{y}\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\int - e^{- 2 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\int e^{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int - e^{- 2 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ e^{y} & =\\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ne^{y}=\\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\ln{\\left(C + \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2} \\right)}.\n$$\n\nThe logarithm argument must be positive on the solution interval; $C$ is an arbitrary real constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["88407400-d880-51d2-a70f-2e5e595f4faa"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "8fe94f93-9195-5b19-a02c-bdfda83b3401" :answer/id #uuid "8fe94f93-9195-5b19-a02c-bdfda83b3401" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C + 8 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2d258e30-3d6d-563a-8e22-e40f19619bec" :answer/id #uuid "2d258e30-3d6d-563a-8e22-e40f19619bec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=C + \\frac{4 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{3}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8326b7c5-af1b-5b98-acb4-56a14bab405e" :answer/id #uuid "8326b7c5-af1b-5b98-acb4-56a14bab405e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C - \\frac{8 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{3}}{3}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ff007452-3669-5b86-be23-b90eb6bb7e32" :answer/id #uuid "ff007452-3669-5b86-be23-b90eb6bb7e32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C + \\frac{8 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{3}}