ion to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ne^{y}=2 e^{- 2 x}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\ln{\\left(C + 2 e^{- 2 x} \\right)}.\n$$\n\nThe logarithm argument must be positive on the solution interval; $C$ is an arbitrary real constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["b58179cf-e8c5-5fe4-81b8-8f5378386268"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "ac4dab2e-343a-53fd-97ec-bf705d967af5" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186068840.py"} [:db/add 17592186068840 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186068840 :knowledge-point/questions ["e1bf8ae5-5934-5cc9-9596-ee1587453d65" "16bf90c3-d378-588a-9105-03dc1e2fe7d8" "c36638cc-24f6-505b-b8ac-375828a36d26" "63e2b730-0d9e-5375-bfbb-085f883671f1" "6fa1db63-f18e-583d-ab37-46117a1bf486" "682503a5-3ea4-50fd-b2dd-c4f6cf554fa9"]} [:db/ensure 17592186068840 :knowledge-point/validate]]
